---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import ExamShell from "../../components/ExamShell.astro";
import ExamPractice from "../../components/ExamPractice.astro";
import ExamFormat from "../../components/ExamFormat.astro";
import formate from "../../data/pruefungen/testdaf-formate.json";

// TEF and TEF Canada: format, results, versions and practice (content-plan §2: the testdaf slot).
// Figures come from testdaf-formate.json; every figure is marked "to verify" there and on the page.
const { bands, modalities } = formate;
---
<Layout
  title="TEF and TEF Canada: format, scores and practice – icanspeak French"
  description="The TEF and TEF Canada, French tests from CCI Paris Île-de-France: what they test, how scores are matched to CEFR levels, and free practice."
>
  <ExamShell
    bild="testdaf"
    header="TEF"
    title="TEF and TEF Canada"
    lead="The French tests of CCI Paris Île-de-France, from A1 to C2. Each paper gets a score that is matched to a CEFR level, and TEF Canada results also to Canadian levels. There is no pass mark."
    leadKey="testdaf.lead"
    badges={["A1–C2"]}
    practiceHeading="Practise for the TEF"
    practiceHeadingKey="testdaf.practiceHeading"
  >
    <Fragment slot="info">
      <section class="exam-section">
        <h2 data-i18n="testdaf.who.title">Who is the TEF for?</h2>
        <div class="exam-meta-row">
          <span class="exam-meta-badge" data-i18n="testdaf.who.badge.result">Result: scores and CEFR levels</span>
          <span class="exam-meta-badge" data-i18n="testdaf.who.badge.oneFormat">One test, levels A1–C2</span>
        </div>
        <p data-i18n="testdaf.who.text">
          The TEF (Test d'évaluation de français) is run by CCI Paris Île-de-France and taken at approved
          centres. TEF Canada is the version accepted for Canadian immigration and citizenship procedures.
          People also take the TEF for study and work, and a version for residence and nationality in
          France exists (to verify). Whether a result is accepted depends on the institution or procedure,
          so check before you book.
        </p>
        <p><a class="plan-link" href="/examens/delf-tcf-ou-tef" data-i18n="testdaf.whichExam">DELF, TCF or TEF? Compare them by purpose →</a></p>
      </section>

      {formate.formate.map((f) => <ExamFormat format={f} />)}

      <section class="exam-section">
        <h2 data-i18n="testdaf.bands.title">How results work</h2>
        <p data-i18n="testdaf.bands.text">
          Each paper is scored on its own, and the report matches each score to a level, so your levels can
          differ from skill to skill. The score ranges and level boundaries are published by the test
          organiser. We don't copy them here because they can change (to verify).
        </p>
        <div class="format-table-wrap">
          <table class="format-table">
            <thead><tr>
              <th data-i18n="testdaf.bands.col.paper">Paper</th>
              <th data-i18n="testdaf.bands.col.marked">Marked by</th>
              <th data-i18n="testdaf.bands.col.result">What you get</th>
            </tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {bands.rows.map((r) => (
                <tr>{r.map((c, i) => (i === 0 ? <th scope="row">{c}</th> : <td>{c}</td>))}</tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="format-note" data-i18n="testdaf.bands.note">
          There is no pass mark: you always get scores. Reading and listening are marked automatically; whether
          wrong answers cost points is to verify, so answer everything unless your centre says otherwise.
          Writing and speaking go to trained raters. TEF Canada results are also converted to NCLC levels
          (to verify).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="exam-section">
        <h2 data-i18n="testdaf.mod.title">TEF, TEF Canada or TEF IRN?</h2>
        <p data-i18n="testdaf.mod.text">
          These are the versions learners ask about most. They differ in which papers you sit and in who
          accepts them. TEF IRN is the version for residence and nationality procedures in France; we only
          mention it here and have no practice set for it (check its current format). Before you book, ask the
          institution which version it accepts.
        </p>
        <div class="format-table-wrap">
          <table class="format-table">
            <thead><tr>
              <th data-i18n="testdaf.mod.th.name">Version</th>
              <th data-i18n="testdaf.mod.th.tests">Papers</th>
              <th data-i18n="testdaf.mod.th.count">Number</th>
              <th data-i18n="testdaf.mod.th.result">You get</th>
            </tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {modalities.map((m) => (
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row" translate="no">{m.id}</th>
                  <td data-i18n={`testdaf.mod.${m.id}.tests`}>{m.tests}</td>
                  <td>{m.points}</td>
                  <td data-i18n={`testdaf.mod.result.${m.result}`}>{m.result}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="exam-section">
        <h2 data-i18n="testdaf.day.title">On the day</h2>
        <ul class="task-points">
          <li data-i18n="testdaf.day.1">Centres differ: some test on paper, some on a computer, and some papers may not let you go back. Ask your centre (to verify).</li>
          <li data-i18n="testdaf.day.2">Listening is multiple choice on a recording. Read the questions before it starts if the rules allow it.</li>
          <li data-i18n="testdaf.day.3">In the speaking paper you talk with an examiner in two role plays. Keep the register each task asks for: tu or vous.</li>
          <li data-i18n="testdaf.day.4">In writing, count your words if a minimum is given, and keep one register from start to finish.</li>
          <li data-i18n="testdaf.day.5">Results come some weeks after the test (to verify). Keep your original document: institutions often check it.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="format-note" data-i18n="testdaf.format.note">
          We aren't connected with the TEF or with CCI Paris Île-de-France, and all our practice material is
          our own. The details here come from public descriptions and may be out of date: treat every number as
          to verify. Check the current rules, prices and the version you need with your test centre or the
          official TEF pages.
        </p>
      </section>
    </Fragment>

    <div class="mock-cta mock-cta--lead">
      <h2 data-i18n="testdaf.set.title">Practise reading and writing</h2>
      <p data-i18n-html="testdaf.set.text">
        Three reading tasks from about B1 to C1, plus a letter or argument task with structure, useful
        phrases and a checklist, in the style of the TEF written papers but shorter. All texts and tasks are
        written by us, not official exam material.
      </p>
      <a class="quiz-btn quiz-btn--primary" href="/tef/serie-d-entrainement" data-i18n="exam.startSet">Start the practice set</a>
    </div>

    <div class="mock-cta">
      <h2 data-i18n="testdaf.bands.cta.title">Practise every task type</h2>
      <p data-i18n="testdaf.bands.cta.text">
        Our TCF sets by level hold all four skills, from A1 to C1. The TCF and the TEF test the same
        skills, so they are good practice for either.
      </p>
      <a class="quiz-btn quiz-btn--primary" href="/tcf" data-i18n="testdaf.bands.cta.link">To the TCF sets by level</a>
    </div>

    <ExamPractice
      heading="Train the basics"
      headingKey="exam.practice.heading"
      intro="Besides the practice sets above, these three tools help at every level and for every exam. They test general articles, grammar and vocabulary, not anything TEF-specific."
      introKey="testdaf.practice.intro"
      tools={["artikel", "grammatik", "wortschatz"]}
    />
  </ExamShell>
</Layout>
